#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Clover Vale: a tile-based adventure of magic ponies, friendship and the
Lantern Festival, in Python + Tk.

Standard library only.  The engine is the one Miskatonic, Hyperspace
Homeroom and Penultimate share (one hero, a map of squares, people to talk
to by keyword, shops, places underneath), and the rules are those of the
pony roleplaying game: four Essences, Skills rated as dice from d2 to d12, a
d20 plus the Skill die against a Difficulty, Friendship Points, magic that
tires you out, and monsters that would often rather be friends.

Clover Vale, the week before the Lantern Festival.  Every Midsummer the
ponies of the valley light the Great Lantern in the Lantern Hall, and its
light keeps the Greymist (a fog that drains the colour and the cheer out of
everything it touches) back in the hills for another year.  This year
someone has stolen the Lantern's four Heartstones and hidden them about the
valley.  Find them, bring them to Grandmare Thistlewick at the Star Tower,
and light the Great Lantern on Lantern Night, Saturday, between sunset and
midnight.  One of the town's grown-ups is not what they seem.

Every new game makes a new week: the Heartstones lie in four of six places
(the old gem mine, the Hollow Wood, the Cloud Castle, the grotto under Lily
Lake, the Clockwork Attic and the ruins of Thornwall Keep), the ponies of
Clover Vale change, and one of them is a Gloom in disguise.  The valley stays
where it is.  The game is saved to ~/.clovervale.json whenever you change
place and when you quit, and resumed next time.

Ponies
  Be a meadow pony, a pegasus or a unicorn, with a Calling (the talent your
  heartmark shows) and a Heart (the virtue you live by).  Twelve points go
  between Strength, Speed, Smarts and Social, and your Origin and Heart add
  four more; each Essence's points become ranks in its Skills.  To do
  something hard, roll a d20 and the Skill's die against a Difficulty (10
  routine, 15 challenging, 20 difficult); with no rank in the Skill you roll
  two d20s and keep the worse.  Upshifts and downshifts move the Skill die up
  and down the ladder; Edge rolls two d20s and keeps the better.

Health and friendship
  A hit costs Health.  At zero you are Defeated: too worn out to go on, for a
  few turns, and then you pick yourself up.  Defeated three times in one
  place and somepony carries you to the Healer's.  Friendship Points, earned
  by living by your Heart and by fumbling gloriously, buy you a pep talk, a
  hint, or a run of luck.  Most monsters can be befriended instead of
  fought (T), and the Heartstones' guardians are no exception.

Talking
  Walk into a pony, or into a counter with someone behind it, then choose or
  type a word.  Everypony knows NAME, JOB and BYE; most know NEWS, and words
  in CAPITALS are worth asking about.  Shopkeepers answer BUY.  Help somepony
  and they become your friend: ask a friend to COME along.

Touch and mouse
  Tap a square to walk there, tap next to you to step, and tap the menus.
  Gamepad (Linux, the Steam Deck): the d-pad or stick moves, A waits or
  chooses, B backs out, X throws, Y uses a talent or spell, LB uses
  something, RB the journal, View the map and Start the menu.

Sound effects and music are synthesized and played with afplay (macOS),
paplay or aplay if one is available, on Android with pyjnius, or with
pygame's mixer; otherwise the game is silent.  Music is cached in
~/.cache/clovervale.

App bundle (macOS):  clovervale --build-app [DIR]   builds clovervale.app
                     clovervale --icon-png SIZE [OUT.png]

Keys
  Arrows/WASD move, Space waits, E searches, F throws, T befriends, C uses a
  talent or a spell, U uses something, I shows your pony, J the journal, M
  the map, ? help.

The tiles are drawn by the code below (PONY_SHAPES, ART and draw_terrain).
--selftest builds every map, room, level and tune of a few weeks without
opening a window.
"""

